====Usage notes====
In Chinese culture, upside-down {{zh-l|*春}} is often used on [[w:Fai chun|CNY decorations]] and symbolizes the arrival of spring after a homophonic pun: {{zh-l|*春}}{{zh-l|倒|dào|inverted}} = {{zh-l|*春}}{{zh-l|到|to arrive}}.

