===Etymology 1===
; used in names of rivers
: From {{bor|zh|bo|ཆུ||river}}.

; to bend, bent, curved, crooked, wrong
: From {{inh|zh|sit-pro|*kəwk||bend, crooked, return, back, year}} (STEDT under PTB *(k/ʔ)uk). Cognate with {{cog|bo|འགུགས||to bend}}, {{cog|my|ကောက်||bent, curved, crooked}} ({{zh-ref|Hill, 2019}}). Compare {{cog|mkh-pro|*gɔk||be crooked, bent, lame}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}).

; song
: Of {{unc|zh|nocap=1}} origin. ''{{w|Shuowen}}'' claims that it derives from the "turn" sense as describing a melodic contour (compare, for example, English's use of {{m|en|turn|id=musical figure}} to describe a musical figure), but most modern scholars doubt this connection, mostly interpreting the depicted bent object as a wind instrument instead. However, a number of other suggestions have been put forth—a rice container, a basket, a tract of farmland, and so on—which, if correct, would invalidate any obvious direct link between shape and sense. In that case, phonetic borrowing is a likely possibility.

; mocking; ridiculing
: From {{zh-m|曲線}}.

